Approaching the Hill~
   At this point you find a set of steps cut into the side of the hill,
allowing for an easy ascent to the Steading itself, should you so wish.  Birds
of prey circle far overhead, as if, having observed such behavior before, they
are expecting an imminent feast.  The steps are much larger than even a troll
would need, and progress would be quite tricky for a halfling, who would have
to literally climb each one.  This is another indication of the giantish nature
of the inhabitants of the Steading.    
